 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+Cache replacement uses the 2Q eviction algorithm to resist sequential screening scans while retaining repeatedly accessed comparison sheets:
+- **FIFO Queue ($A1$ / In)**: Newly rendered previews enter a FIFO queue upon admission.
+- **LRU Queue ($Am$ / Main)**: If a requested preview is hit while resident in $A1$ (or referenced on subsequent access), it is promoted to the frequency/recency queue ($Am$). Subsequent hits in $Am$ move the entry to the most-recently-used position.
+- **Queue Sizing & Eviction**: Total cache capacity is bounded at 12 GiB, split between $A1$ and $Am$ (e.g. 25% $A1$ budget, 75% $Am$ budget). When cache space is exhausted prior to admitting a new sheet, entries are evicted from $A1$ first; if $A1$ is below its minimum threshold or empty, entries are evicted from the LRU tail of $Am$.
+- Eviction metadata is maintained strictly in memory within the preview worker and discarded on restart; cached files are validated against the bounds on boot.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Cache Eviction Policy | 2Q (Two-Queue Eviction) | LRU, Frequency-based eviction with aging | 2Q buffers newly rendered previews in a FIFO queue before promotion to an LRU queue, protecting repeatedly referenced comparison sheets from eviction during long sequential screenings without the stale-counter overhead of LFU. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. ✅ Eviction policy selected: 2Q eviction policy chosen to protect comparison sheets against sequential screening scans.
+
+### Deferred
+1. Concrete partition threshold between $A1$ and $Am$ queues under production load (initial target: 25% $A1$ / 75% $Am$).
